  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "${(2a-{b}^{2})}^{2}=$",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(x-y)^{2}={x}^{2}-2xy+{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2a$ and $y={b}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(2a-{b}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ (2a)^{2}-2(2a)({b}^{2})+{({b}^{2})}^{2} & = \\\\ 4{a}^{2}-4a{b}^{2}+{b}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
